20:33:46.649 advertise: AUTO - each client is told the host it can actually reach:
20:33:46.649   a client on a private, loopback, link-local or CGNAT address is told the
20:33:46.649   address it reached this server on; a client on a public address is told
20:33:46.649   this box's public address, below.
20:33:46.649   public address: 203.0.113.42 (from checkip.amazonaws.com, re-checked every 10 min)
20:33:46.649   channel 0: port 8485, host decided per connection
20:33:46.649   channel 1: port 8486, host decided per connection
20:33:46.649 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
20:33:46.649   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
20:33:46.649 THIS CHANNEL ANSWERS PACKETS - the default since 2026-09-14. It used to need
20:33:46.649   --set-field-probe, a flag every caller passed and whose absence cost a launch;
20:33:46.650   --silent-channel is the way to turn answering off now, and it is only for
20:33:46.650   eliminating the channel as a variable.
20:33:46.650   This channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
20:33:46.650   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
20:33:46.650   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
20:33:46.650   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
20:33:46.650   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
20:33:46.650   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
20:33:46.650   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
20:33:46.650   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
20:33:46.650   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
